# One calculation, many screens

If more than one component needs the same number (goals, units, leftover, revenue, %), put the math in a shared module and have every screen call it. Do not copy the formula into each Vue file.

## Campaign month progress (My results / Team results)

Public front door: `getCampaignMonthView` in [`src/js/orderAuthority.js`](src/js/orderAuthority.js). Implementation helpers live in [`src/js/statsUtils.js`](src/js/statsUtils.js) and are re-exported from orderAuthority.

Vue screens, the store, and copy helpers import campaign math from `orderAuthority.js`, not from `statsUtils.js`.

If My results, Team results, leftover, or monthly breakdowns look wrong, change `getCampaignMonthView` (or the statsUtils helpers it calls). Do not patch `agentDashboard.vue`, `assignGoals.vue`, `agentCaseCard.vue`, `agentsPage.vue`, or reports separately.

Call it like:

```js
const view = getCampaignMonthView(order, dailyLogs, monthKey, agentId)
// view.myUnits / view.myGoal   — personal
// view.teamUnits / view.teamGoal — team
// view.monthlyBreakdown        — calendar month buckets
```

Do not call `calculateMonthlyProgress` from Vue. Use `view.monthlyBreakdown`.

Month buckets are local calendar `YYYY-MM` / `YYYY-MM-DD`. Never use `toISOString()` for those strings (it shifts the day in UTC+).

Leftover hours stay with the agent who still has unused assignment. Never split leftover or auto-assign it to anyone else — see `.cursor/rules/leftover-stays-with-agent.mdc`.

## When adding a new screen

- Import the existing helper from `orderAuthority.js`. If it is missing a field, extend the view object and reuse it.
- Vue components format and render. They do not invent leftover, scaling, or month-cap logic.
- Per-log unit extraction (`getLogCompletedUnits`) is fine for weekly tables and A-leads rows. Campaign leftover / goal / month totals still go through `getCampaignMonthView`.
- New campaign math goes in `statsUtils.js` and is exposed through `orderAuthority.js`.
